Versa generator monitor outputs on X3
------------------------------------

Configurable or fixed GMII generator instance 0 drives these complementary
3.3 V output pairs (no monitor outputs in PRBS mode):

    Signal        X3 positive   X3 negative   FPGA positive / negative
    cycle_start   pin 7         pin 8         E6 / D6 (PT6A / PT6B)
    gmii_en       pin 9         pin 10        E7 / D7 (PT9A / PT9B)

Both use LVCMOS33D, DRIVE=12 and SLEWRATE=FAST. Trellis configures each
pair through its A pad; the B pad is driven automatically and must not
receive a separate top-level output buffer.

For the discussed Tektronix 11801B trigger connection, use ONLY the positive
output through an external 330 ohm series resistor near the header, then
50 ohm coax into the scope's 50 ohm direct trigger input. Connect board
ground to the coax shield and leave the negative output unconnected. Select
x1, DC coupling and a trigger level around 0.2 V. The resistor is external
and required; FPGA constraints do not provide attenuation.

Validation: generated the full serdes_64data_20gap SoC and checked monitor
connections, pin/drive constraints and nonempty BIOS initialization. A
separate minimal design using the same two pairs routed successfully; its
configuration sets both A/B drivers to 12 mA. The full routed result is
recorded below. The timing-passing image has now been programmed; see below.


