The BIOS-inclusive serdes_64data_20gap design with cycle_start on X3:7/8 and
gmii_en on X3:9/10 routed and packed successfully. Final RX131.03 MHz PASS125,
TX218.29 MHz PASS125, SYS93.05 MHz PASS75.0075. All timing.json clocks pass.
Use the current prog/versa_ecp5_sequence_region.py: rectangle (20,35)-(45,70),
687 cells in this build, seed1/router1/speed8. BIOS initialization was verified
in mapped ROM BRAMs. Both bitstream and SVF are saved with all implementation
inputs and reports at codex/reports/versa-monitors-routed. This supersedes
the earlier zero-ROM timing result and the 122.17 MHz boot diagnostic.
The new image was programmed over USB JTAG on 2026-11-09. UART boot,
RAM test and LiteX prompt passed. Monitor waveforms and packet reception
have not yet been verified with this image. Flash was not programmed.


Versa SERDES diagnostic status register
--------------------------------------

Dedicated SERDES modes now expose the read-only 32-bit serdes_status CSR
in a separate system-clock bank. In the generated 32-bit-CSR fixed64/20
configuration it is at 0x82004000:

    mem_read 0x82004000 4  # serdes_status (NEW image only)

    Bit  Field                 Meaning when 1
     0   ref_pll_locked         Fabric reference-clock PLL locked
     1   tx_pll_locked          DCU TX PLL locked (inverted PLOL)
     2   rx_cdr_locked          DCU RX CDR locked (inverted RLOL)
     3   rx_signal_detected     DCU does not report loss of signal
     4   tx_ready               TX initialization settled
     5   rx_ready               RX initialization settled
     6   cdr_ready              Filtered CDR-ready condition used by PCS
     7   pcs_synced             PCS has code-group synchronization
     8   tx_reset               TX GMII datapath reset asserted
     9   rx_pcs_reset           RX PCS reset asserted
    10   rx_mac_reset           RX analyzer/MAC reset asserted
    11   serdes_reset           DCU startup reset asserted
    12   tx_clock_active        Recent TX clock activity
    13   rx_clock_active        Recent RX clock activity
    14   rx_enabled             Receive logic instantiated
 15-31   reserved              Zero

All asynchronous flags are synchronized into sys. Clock-activity dividers
continue during datapath reset; flags expire after 4095 sys-clock cycles
without a synchronized transition (about 54.6 us at 75 MHz). These flags
indicate activity, not clock frequency or jitter. They recover when clocks
restart. In TX-only builds RX lock/ready/activity flags are zero, RX resets
are one and rx_enabled is zero. A healthy full link normally reads 0x70ff.

The BIOS and CSR map must match the new image: adding the diagnostic bank
moves timer0 to 0x82005000 and UART to 0x82006000 in this configuration.
Analyzer addresses stay unchanged. Use that build's generated csr.csv.
The original monitor-only image predates this CSR and maps timer0 at
0x82004000 instead. The currently programmed corrected status image uses
the new map; hardware validation is recorded below.

Validation includes every status bit, activity during reset, stopped RX
clock detection, clock restart, and TX-only elaboration without RX clocks.


