Versa corrected status readback and hardware lock (2026-11-09)
-----------------------------------------------------------

The initial status build had a CSR wiring error: declaring fields while
driving the packed status signal let LiteX override it with undriven fields.
It returned zero even for constant rx_enabled. Corrected by driving fields
individually; regression now includes finalized CSR wiring and CPU read word.
All6 ECP5 tests pass. Rebuilt with identical CSR addresses and explicit
matching BIOS. Final routed RX127.37 PASS125, TX179.05 PASS125,
SYS87.56 PASS75.0075; seed2/router1/current expanded region.

Programmed corrected image, verified BIOS/RAM test/prompt. Five reads of
serdes_status all0x747f: reference PLL, TX PLL, RX CDR locked; signal present;
TX/RX ready and both clocks active. PCS synchronization remains0, so RX MAC
and analyzer are held in reset(bit10=1). The clock lock check passes, but
packet reception remains unresolved at PCS synchronization. Current board
image is archived in codex/reports/versa-serdes-status-fixed with mapped
inputs, BIOS/CSR map, timing, bitstream/SVF and hardware transcripts.


Versa channel rate correction and measured clocks (2026-11-09)
-----------------------------------------------------------

The user's approximately336ns gmii_en period suggested250MHz GMII. The
20x125MHz DCU profile was missing explicit per-channel half-rate selection,
despite /2 divider attributes. Set both TX/RX RATE_MODE parameters and
FFC_RATE_MODE controls to1. No generator pattern changes. Added read-only
serdes_tx_clock_count at0x82004004 and serdes_rx_clock_count at0x82004008;
existing serdes_status remains0x82004000. Counts measure edges per65536
syscycles with resetless Gray counters, independent of PCS/datapath reset.

    mem_read 0x82004000 4  # serdes_status
    mem_read 0x82004004 4  # serdes_tx_clock_count
    mem_read 0x82004008 4  # serdes_rx_clock_count

FrequencyHz=count*sys_clk_freq/65536. Wait a complete window after reset.
At75MHz sys, expected count109226/109227 for125MHz,218453/218454 for250MHz.
Hardware after programming: five TX/RX samples109226/109227, approximately
125.000MHz. Expected gmii_en period672ns (high576ns/low96ns); external scope
confirmation pending. Status0x747f unchanged: clockslocked, but PCSsync0 and
analyzerheldreset. No received packets. Six tests pass, including clock-rate
measurement and672ns digital-model period. Final RX130.50PASS125,
TX177.78PASS125, SYS83.46PASS75.0075. Current programmed image and matching
artifacts/transcripts: codex/reports/versa-rate-fix. Flash unchanged.


