Versa TX serializer synchronization fix (2026-11-10)
--------------------------------------------------

Explicitly enable D_SYNC_LOCAL_EN=0b1 in the project DCUA wrapper. Leaving
local serializer synchronization disabled allowed TX PLL lock and its SMA
clock-test output, while TX_PCLK and normal serial data remained flat.
CH1_TX_CM_SEL=0b01 also explicitly enables the 0.6V common-mode setting.
The imported LiteICLink profile itself is unchanged.

Hardware now measures raw DCU TX_PCLK125MHz; user confirms normal SMA
output transitions. Internal serial TX-to-RX loopback achieves PCS sync:
packet counter1158596->3518467 with zero CRC/preamble errors. Afterwards
loopback disabled, normal serial DATA selected, externalRXrecovered with
zero CRC/preamble errors. TX fabric retains the internal125MHzreference.

Current SRAM image:codex/reports/versa-tx-sync/lattice_versa_ecp5.svf.
It reuses the timing-passing versa-tx-refclk routing, changing only two DCU
configuration words (commonmode andlocalsync), then repacking. Matching
CSR/BIOS/timing/config/logs archived alongside. Source fixes are included
in subsequent normal builds. Physical SMA TX-to-RX cable test remains.

Physical SMA cable loopback subsequently verified: internal loopbackOFF,
PCSsync1, TX/RX125MHz, +4262278receivedpackets, zeroCRC/preambleerrors.
Matching transcript and JSON:codex/reports/versa-tx-sync/versa-sma-loopback-*.
